1
00:00:02,450 --> 00:00:04,375
{\an8}Now, the Apps panel.

2
00:00:04,950 --> 00:00:08,475
{\an8}On the dash, the nine-dot button in the dock opens it.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,100
{\an8}You set it up on the Apps panel page.

4
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,850
{\an8}It slides in over the dash, and it has a fixed size.

5
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:23,800
{\an8}You build it like a dash, with cards and widgets.

6
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:29,550
{\an8}To add something, click Add to the panel.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,550
{\an8}You'll find quick settings and apps, and a Controls card.

8
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:38,725
{\an8}Further down: phone widgets, OBD sensors, and New column.

9
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,700
{\an8}A new card is filled with a widget automatically.

10
00:00:46,400 --> 00:00:49,800
{\an8}Change it as you like, or remove it if you don't want it.

11
00:00:53,850 --> 00:00:57,025
{\an8}Each click on Buttons adds another Buttons card.

12
00:00:59,050 --> 00:01:02,450
{\an8}The panel's space is fixed, so use it wisely.

13
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:09,925
{\an8}Click a card to see its options.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:13,700
{\an8}The Apps card shows apps from your phone.

15
00:01:19,550 --> 00:01:21,350
{\an8}Choose what it shows:

16
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:26,475
{\an8}apps on the head unit, in the same order as on your phone,

17
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:30,175
{\an8}or only your music apps.

18
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:35,050
{\an8}Last opened keeps the apps you use most at the front.

19
00:01:37,650 --> 00:01:40,650
{\an8}If a card gets too small, give it more space.

20
00:01:43,650 --> 00:01:45,950
{\an8}Or remove a card to make room.

21
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:51,250
{\an8}Click a Buttons card to see its buttons.

22
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:55,925
{\an8}Each click on Add button adds one more, until the card is full.

23
00:01:57,100 --> 00:02:02,150
{\an8}Every button has the usual options: what it does, text, icon and look.

24
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:06,925
{\an8}It's a lot at first, so play with it. You can't break anything.

25
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:15,300
{\an8}To keep your current dash, save under a new name, or click Discard.
